WEBVTT

02:21.892 --> 02:24.770
Is it possible that the water
has already killed them?

02:25.187 --> 02:27.148
Yes.

02:27.231 --> 02:28.774
Then what?

02:29.984 --> 02:31.777
If it doesn't work?

04:04.662 --> 04:06.163
Get them in the truck.

04:07.123 --> 04:09.250
Get the hoses in! Start pumping!

04:25.724 --> 04:28.644
Uh, I'm here to see
my husband, Vasily Ignatenko.

04:28.727 --> 04:31.188
He's a firefighter from Chernobyl.
I have permission.

04:31.397 --> 04:33.774
Chernobyl? I'm sorry, no visitors.

04:36.068 --> 04:38.487
Well, but Major...
Major Burov told me,

04:38.571 --> 04:39.905
- he said...
- No exceptions.

04:39.989 --> 04:42.783
Please. I've come all the way
from Kievskaya Oblast.

05:08.893 --> 05:10.603
Excuse me.

05:11.937 --> 05:13.397
Excuse me, excuse me.

05:13.481 --> 05:14.773
Who are you? What are you doing here?

05:14.857 --> 05:17.651
- I have a pass.
- You can't be here. It's not safe.

05:17.735 --> 05:19.612
I am here to see my husband.

05:19.695 --> 05:20.696
Vasily Ignatenko.

05:20.779 --> 05:22.281
He's a firefighter from Chernobyl.

05:22.364 --> 05:24.825
I know who Ignatenko is,
but you can't.

05:24.909 --> 05:26.911
I have permission. I've...

05:33.209 --> 05:36.587
You can see him for 30 minutes,
not a minute more.

05:36.670 --> 05:39.465
And you cannot touch him in any way.
Do you understand?

05:39.548 --> 05:41.800
- Yeah.
- Room 15.

05:43.552 --> 05:44.553
Thank you.

05:45.179 --> 05:47.056
- You're not pregnant, are you?
- No.

05:54.980 --> 05:56.649
I won't have
to give that to you.

05:56.732 --> 05:57.775
There they are.

05:58.192 --> 05:59.777
No, wait, wait, wait.
I haven't finished yet.

05:59.860 --> 06:00.986
No, no, he hasn't.

06:01.779 --> 06:03.113
Yeah, that's good.

06:05.991 --> 06:07.243
Yeah, better.

06:10.162 --> 06:11.872
Look who the cat dragged in.

06:14.500 --> 06:16.168
What did I tell you?

06:17.002 --> 06:19.338
There's no hiding from you,
is there? Eh?

06:22.675 --> 06:24.677
Easy, easy. It's okay.

06:24.760 --> 06:28.055
We're all okay. Yeah, we're okay.

07:38.042 --> 07:41.545
How, how, how did this happen?
Who gave them the idea?

07:41.629 --> 07:43.505
- Are you suggesting I did?
- Someone did.

07:43.589 --> 07:47.092
Someone decided
that the evacuation zone

07:47.176 --> 07:50.346
should be 30 kilometers,
when we know, here,

07:50.429 --> 07:53.182
cesium-137 in the Gomel district.

07:53.265 --> 07:55.893
- That's 200 kilometers away!
- It was decided.

07:55.976 --> 07:57.895
- Based on what?
- I don't know!

07:59.355 --> 08:03.275
Forgive me. Maybe I... I've just
spent too much time in my lab.

08:03.359 --> 08:05.027
Or maybe I'm just stupid.

08:05.819 --> 08:07.571
Is this really the way it all works?

08:08.697 --> 08:10.574
An uninformed, arbitrary decision

08:10.658 --> 08:12.910
that will cost who knows
how many lives

08:12.993 --> 08:16.872
made by some apparatchik?
Some career party man?

08:18.957 --> 08:21.043
I'm a career party man.

08:22.002 --> 08:24.797
You should watch your tone,
Comrade Legasov.

08:25.923 --> 08:27.091
Comrades...

08:28.133 --> 08:30.803
We have visual confirmation
that the fire is nearly extinguished.

08:30.886 --> 08:32.888
There has also been
a reduction in iodine-131

08:32.971 --> 08:34.807
and cesium-137 emissions.

08:34.890 --> 08:36.517
Good. Yes?

08:37.309 --> 08:40.145
But the temperature is rising.

08:40.229 --> 08:41.605
And, uh...

08:48.779 --> 08:51.657
There's a spike
in zirconium-95.

08:52.991 --> 08:56.203
It's from the cladding
on the fuel rods.

08:56.286 --> 08:58.622
Meaning what?

08:58.706 --> 09:01.083
The meltdown has begun.

09:39.705 --> 09:41.248
Get it off me!

09:43.876 --> 09:46.253
Get it off me!

09:53.761 --> 09:55.262
Stop moving!

09:55.345 --> 09:58.098
Get off him! You're hurting him!

09:58.932 --> 10:01.059
- You can't be in here.
- What's happening to him?

10:01.143 --> 10:02.603
Get out!

10:02.686 --> 10:04.438
You can't be in here!

10:47.397 --> 10:48.398
Yes?

10:48.482 --> 10:49.983
Comrade Shcherbina
is on the phone.

10:50.067 --> 10:51.443
Put him through.

10:52.903 --> 10:54.196
Well?

10:54.279 --> 10:55.948
The fire's nearly out.

10:56.031 --> 10:57.783
The bubbler tanks are being drained.

10:57.866 --> 11:00.828
We have successfully eliminated
the risk of a thermal explosion.

11:04.039 --> 11:05.040
And?

11:06.542 --> 11:08.168
The situation inside the core

11:08.252 --> 11:11.129
is deteriorating
faster than anticipated.

11:11.213 --> 11:14.091
The concrete pad will last
for six to eight weeks,

11:14.174 --> 11:17.219
but after that, Legasov estimates
a 50% chance

11:17.302 --> 11:19.012
that the fuel will breach the pad

11:19.096 --> 11:21.807
and melt down
into the groundwater itself.

11:22.766 --> 11:25.310
And where
does this groundwater go?

11:25.394 --> 11:27.437
The Pripyat River,

11:27.521 --> 11:30.440
which feeds into the Dnieper.

11:30.524 --> 11:33.902
The primary water supply for
approximately 50 million people,

11:33.986 --> 11:38.115
not to mention crops and livestock,
would be unusable.

11:38.198 --> 11:40.909
We're recommending we install
a heat exchanger under the pad

11:40.993 --> 11:44.079
to lower the core temperature
and halt the meltdown.

11:44.162 --> 11:47.207
And in order to do that,
I'm told that we will need

11:49.543 --> 11:53.380
all of the liquid nitrogen
in the Soviet Union.

11:55.841 --> 11:56.842
Oh.

11:58.010 --> 11:59.094
All right.

11:59.177 --> 12:00.762
Yeah, and of course,
we'll also need...

12:00.846 --> 12:02.139
Whatever you need, you have it.

12:02.222 --> 12:03.640
- That should be clear by now.
- Yes.

12:03.724 --> 12:05.309
- Anything else?
- Uh, no, no, no. Thank you.

12:05.392 --> 12:08.437
Yes. I'd like to address
the 30-kilometer exclusion zone.

12:08.520 --> 12:11.273
Wait, what?
Professor Legasov, is that you?

12:11.356 --> 12:12.608
What exclusion zone?

12:12.691 --> 12:14.735
Minor details, General Secretary.

12:14.818 --> 12:17.362
Um, Premier Ryzhkov
has determined that...

12:17.446 --> 12:19.823
If he determined, then he determined.

12:19.907 --> 12:21.325
Look, Professor Legasov,

12:21.408 --> 12:23.327
you are there for one reason only.

12:23.410 --> 12:25.454
Do you understand? To make this stop.

12:25.537 --> 12:26.747
I don't want questions.

12:26.830 --> 12:28.457
I want to know when this will be over.

12:28.832 --> 12:30.876
If you mean when will
Chernobyl be completely safe,

12:30.959 --> 12:34.129
the half-life of plutonium-239
is 24,000 years.

12:34.212 --> 12:37.382
So perhaps we should just say,
"Not within our lifetimes."

12:49.645 --> 12:51.521
I think you and I should take a walk.

12:52.064 --> 12:53.732
It's late. I'm tired.

12:54.816 --> 12:57.152
We're taking a walk.

13:03.617 --> 13:06.036
What is it you want? An apology?

13:07.829 --> 13:09.539
Not gonna sit back and...

13:11.458 --> 13:13.543
What will happen to our boys?

13:14.461 --> 13:16.880
Which boys? The divers?

13:16.964 --> 13:19.883
The divers, the firefighters,
the men in the control room.

13:20.592 --> 13:23.971
What does the radiation
do to them, precisely?

13:25.681 --> 13:28.308
At the levels
some of them were exposed?

13:28.392 --> 13:31.520
Ionizing radiation tears
the cellular structure apart.

13:32.479 --> 13:35.315
The skin blisters,
turns red, then black.

13:36.984 --> 13:39.486
This is followed by a latency period.

13:40.696 --> 13:42.572
The immediate effects subside.

13:42.656 --> 13:44.408
The patient appears to be recovering.

13:45.617 --> 13:47.995
Healthy, even. But they aren't.

13:49.621 --> 13:52.958
This usually only lasts
for a day or two.

13:55.460 --> 13:56.670
Continue.

13:58.213 --> 14:01.925
Then the cellular damage
begins to manifest.

14:02.009 --> 14:07.389
The bone marrow dies,
the immune system fails,

14:07.472 --> 14:11.184
the organs and soft tissue
begin to decompose.

14:11.268 --> 14:15.313
The arteries and veins
spill open like sieves,

14:15.397 --> 14:17.816
to the point where you can't
even administer morphine

14:17.899 --> 14:21.486
for the pain, which is unimaginable.

14:22.279 --> 14:25.532
And then three days
to three weeks, you're dead.

14:27.784 --> 14:30.037
That is what will happen
to those boys.

14:32.372 --> 14:33.749
And what about us?

14:37.169 --> 14:38.962
Well, we've...

14:39.046 --> 14:42.007
We've gotten a steady dose,
but not as much of it.

14:43.341 --> 14:45.177
Not strong enough to kill the cells,

14:45.260 --> 14:48.305
but consistent enough
to damage our DNA.

14:49.765 --> 14:52.517
So, in time, cancer.

14:53.060 --> 14:56.313
Or aplastic anemia. Either way, fatal.

14:59.066 --> 15:00.358
Well...

15:02.402 --> 15:08.033
In a sense, it would seem we've
gotten off easy then, Valery.

15:20.712 --> 15:22.506
I've seen them before.

15:28.553 --> 15:31.848
Now you know
why I wanted to take a walk.

15:31.932 --> 15:34.184
We can presume
the work site is bugged.

15:35.185 --> 15:39.231
And our rooms, even our bathrooms.

15:39.314 --> 15:41.483
They've been here the whole time.

15:41.566 --> 15:43.568
Of course, they've been here
the whole time.

15:44.820 --> 15:48.698
But if we're seeing them
out in the open now,

15:48.782 --> 15:51.451
it's because they want us to know.

16:33.326 --> 16:34.494
You've seen that?

16:36.955 --> 16:38.999
The fuel is melting
faster than we expected.

16:39.082 --> 16:41.376
I know. I have a plan.

16:42.127 --> 16:44.713
Heat exchanger, I hope.

16:44.796 --> 16:46.256
Yes.

16:49.467 --> 16:51.386
There's something I've wanted
to ask you, comrade,

16:51.469 --> 16:54.848
but I see you're already asking
yourself the same question.

16:58.602 --> 17:00.854
Why did it explode?

17:02.564 --> 17:04.858
I've worked the numbers over and over,

17:04.941 --> 17:08.528
presuming the worst possible
conditions in an RBMK reactor.

17:10.530 --> 17:13.158
And I always get the same answer.

17:13.241 --> 17:14.659
Which is?

17:16.077 --> 17:17.245
It's not possible.

17:18.455 --> 17:19.873
And yet...

17:22.959 --> 17:25.045
You're not going to solve this here.

17:26.713 --> 17:28.215
Not on paper.

17:29.925 --> 17:31.718
Everyone who was in the control room,

17:31.801 --> 17:34.179
Dyatlov, Akimov, Toptunov,

17:34.262 --> 17:37.766
they're all in Moscow,
Hospital Number 6.

17:38.683 --> 17:41.728
We need to find out exactly
what happened that night,

17:41.811 --> 17:45.273
moment by moment,
decision by decision.

17:46.691 --> 17:48.693
Go now while they're still alive.

17:48.777 --> 17:50.987
Talk to them.

17:51.071 --> 17:53.657
Because if we don't find out
how this happened,

17:53.740 --> 17:56.034
it will happen again.

17:59.246 --> 18:00.956
And, Khomyuk...

18:02.332 --> 18:03.959
Be careful.

18:28.525 --> 18:30.068
Well, fuck you!

18:33.029 --> 18:34.990
Hey, here's one, here's one.

18:35.073 --> 18:36.992
What's as big as a house,

18:37.075 --> 18:40.120
burns 20 liters of fuel every hour,

18:40.203 --> 18:42.038
puts out a shit-load of smoke
and noise,

18:43.248 --> 18:45.500
and cuts an apple into three pieces?

18:48.044 --> 18:51.506
A Soviet machine made to cut
apples into four pieces!

19:30.837 --> 19:33.298
- Who's in charge here?
- I'm the crew chief.

19:34.966 --> 19:38.178
I am Shadov,
Minister of Coal Industries.

19:38.261 --> 19:39.554
We know who you are.

19:41.765 --> 19:43.433
How many men do you have?

19:44.017 --> 19:47.520
On this shift, 45 here,
a hundred in total.

19:48.438 --> 19:51.399
I need all 100 men to gather
their equipment and get in the trucks.

19:52.650 --> 19:55.070
Do you? To where?

19:56.821 --> 19:58.031
That's classified.

20:04.746 --> 20:05.914
Come on, then.

20:06.498 --> 20:07.749
Start shooting.

20:08.208 --> 20:10.919
You haven't got enough
bullets for all of us.

20:11.002 --> 20:13.171
Kill as many as you can,
whoever's left,

20:13.505 --> 20:15.131
they'll beat the living piss
out of each of you.

20:15.215 --> 20:17.467
- You can't talk to us like that!
- Shut the fuck up!

20:18.635 --> 20:21.137
This is Tula. This is our mine.

20:22.180 --> 20:23.973
We don't leave unless we know why.

20:26.017 --> 20:27.102
Mmm.

20:31.272 --> 20:33.274
You're going to Chernobyl.

20:35.402 --> 20:36.986
Do you know what's happened there?

20:38.113 --> 20:40.115
We dig up coal, not bodies.

20:41.282 --> 20:43.576
The reactor fuel is going
to sink into the ground

20:43.660 --> 20:46.579
and poison the water
from Kiev to the Black Sea.

20:46.663 --> 20:47.997
All of it.

20:49.124 --> 20:50.625
Forever, they say.

20:52.752 --> 20:55.296
They want you
to stop that from happening.

20:56.673 --> 20:58.842
And how are we supposed to do that?

20:59.676 --> 21:02.303
They didn't tell me,
because I don't need to know.

21:04.264 --> 21:06.766
Do you need to know,
or have you heard enough?

21:48.016 --> 21:50.810
Now you look like
the Minister of Coal.

22:12.373 --> 22:13.791
Vasya?

22:15.251 --> 22:16.503
Vasya?

22:22.675 --> 22:23.885
No, no, no.

22:24.886 --> 22:26.721
They told you no touching.

22:27.222 --> 22:29.474
It's not safe.

22:29.557 --> 22:31.809
They touch you.

22:32.894 --> 22:34.812
If it's safe for them,
it's safe for me.

22:44.906 --> 22:46.741
Where are the others?

22:46.824 --> 22:48.660
They took them to a special room.

22:50.328 --> 22:51.955
They won't tell me where.

22:56.251 --> 22:57.377
Will you open the curtains?

22:58.878 --> 22:59.879
Hmm?

23:00.171 --> 23:01.548
Open the curtains.

23:05.635 --> 23:06.636
Ah.

23:24.195 --> 23:26.364
Please, tell me what you see outside.

23:27.448 --> 23:28.950
Tell me everything.

23:36.457 --> 23:37.458
Um...

23:39.252 --> 23:41.212
I can see the Red Square.

23:44.299 --> 23:45.425
And

23:46.301 --> 23:48.094
the Kremlin.

23:49.387 --> 23:52.557
Spasskaya Tower, the mausoleum.

23:55.018 --> 23:56.686
You see St. Basil's?

23:58.313 --> 23:59.814
Yeah.

23:59.897 --> 24:01.608
Ah.

24:01.899 --> 24:03.610
Yes, it's beautiful.

24:05.153 --> 24:07.113
I told you.

24:07.196 --> 24:09.949
I told you I'd show you Moscow,
didn't I?

24:10.158 --> 24:11.242
Huh?

24:11.326 --> 24:13.328
Yeah. Yes.

24:19.292 --> 24:21.085
Thank you.

25:08.383 --> 25:11.052
I'm not eating that. It's shit.

25:11.886 --> 25:13.096
Get me something else.

25:14.472 --> 25:16.933
I'm not a nurse, Comrade Dyatlov.

25:17.016 --> 25:18.851
I'm a nuclear physicist.

25:19.811 --> 25:22.230
Well, then, Comrade Nuclear Physicist,

25:23.773 --> 25:28.277
unless you happen to have
a butter and caviar sandwich on you,

25:28.361 --> 25:30.697
you can get the fuck out of my room.

26:49.609 --> 26:50.860
What?

26:51.944 --> 26:53.529
I'm not good at this, Boris.

26:54.572 --> 26:56.407
The lying.

27:00.828 --> 27:03.331
Have you ever spent time with miners?

27:05.249 --> 27:06.584
No.

27:06.751 --> 27:09.378
My advice, tell the truth.

27:09.462 --> 27:12.840
These men work in the dark.
They see everything.

27:14.342 --> 27:16.677
Andrei Glukhov, crew chief.

27:32.276 --> 27:33.444
Do these work?

27:35.238 --> 27:36.781
To an extent.

27:40.076 --> 27:41.077
Of course.

27:53.256 --> 27:54.715
So what's the job?

27:56.717 --> 28:00.429
We need to install a liquid
nitrogen heat exchanger

28:00.513 --> 28:03.724
underneath this concrete pad.

28:03.808 --> 28:07.478
There's no way to approach
from the interior of the building,

28:07.562 --> 28:09.897
so you have to get at it
from underground.

28:09.981 --> 28:13.442
- And what's above the pad?
- The core of the nuclear reactor,

28:13.526 --> 28:15.862
which is melting down.

28:17.363 --> 28:19.031
What? Like...

28:20.741 --> 28:21.868
Essentially.

28:23.870 --> 28:25.204
Is it gonna fall on top of us?

28:25.288 --> 28:27.081
Not if you're done within six weeks.

28:29.041 --> 28:31.002
Dimensions?

28:34.046 --> 28:36.007
Break ground here,

28:36.090 --> 28:38.467
dig a tunnel 150 meters to here,

28:38.551 --> 28:41.512
excavate a space 30 by 30 meters

28:41.596 --> 28:43.389
for the heat exchanger.

28:43.472 --> 28:46.559
And because we need to keep disruption
of the ground above to a minimum,

28:46.642 --> 28:48.436
you can't use any heavy machinery.

28:48.519 --> 28:49.937
It has to be done by hand.

28:50.771 --> 28:52.690
Gonna need more men.

28:53.774 --> 28:55.151
Four hundred at least.

28:55.234 --> 28:57.778
We'll have to work around the clock.

28:57.862 --> 28:59.614
How deep do you want this tunnel?
Six meters?

28:59.697 --> 29:02.742
- Twelve.
- Twelve? Why?

29:02.950 --> 29:05.411
For your protection.

29:05.494 --> 29:09.373
At that depth, you'll be shielded
from much of the radiation.

29:10.207 --> 29:13.502
The entrance to the tunnel
won't be 12 meters below ground.

29:14.795 --> 29:16.672
No.

29:16.756 --> 29:19.634
And we're not 12 meters
below ground now.

29:24.347 --> 29:27.224
No. We're not.

29:30.144 --> 29:32.188
We have
some equipment here on site.

29:33.230 --> 29:35.274
More will arrive by midnight.

29:36.817 --> 29:38.194
You can start in the morning.

29:38.277 --> 29:40.154
No. We start now.

29:40.947 --> 29:44.742
I don't want my men here
one more second than they need to be.

29:46.035 --> 29:49.455
If these worked,
you'd be wearing them.

29:59.632 --> 30:01.175
Are they all like that?

30:02.009 --> 30:03.719
They're all like that.

31:27.470 --> 31:28.471
Yes?

31:29.138 --> 31:30.306
What's it up to?

31:30.389 --> 31:31.682
Uh, 50 degrees.

31:35.644 --> 31:36.645
Fuck!

31:41.192 --> 31:42.276
Hey!

31:43.486 --> 31:44.570
Hey, you!

31:54.121 --> 31:55.539
We need fans.

31:55.623 --> 31:57.208
For what purpose?

31:57.541 --> 31:59.043
What do you mean, "For what purpose?"

31:59.126 --> 32:00.920
To dig your fucking tunnel,
that's why.

32:01.003 --> 32:02.797
- Who's talking to you?
- Whoa, whoa. Comrades.

32:04.131 --> 32:05.549
It's 50 degrees down there.

32:06.509 --> 32:09.553
We can't breathe without the masks,
we can't breathe with the masks.

32:09.637 --> 32:12.515
It's like a fucking oven.
We need ventilation.

32:12.598 --> 32:15.518
Fans will put dust in the air,
the dust will go in your lungs.

32:15.601 --> 32:18.104
I've been breathing dust
in my lungs for 20 years.

32:18.187 --> 32:20.981
Not this dust. I'm sorry.

32:21.065 --> 32:23.442
For your own good, no fans.

32:52.388 --> 32:54.723
My name is Ulana Khomyuk.

32:54.807 --> 32:57.643
I'm a nuclear physicist
with the Chernobyl Commission.

32:59.937 --> 33:02.398
I want you to tell me
everything that happened

33:02.481 --> 33:03.691
on the night of the accident.

33:05.401 --> 33:06.569
Is that all right?

33:09.572 --> 33:10.614
Yes.

33:12.950 --> 33:14.160
I want to tell.

33:15.369 --> 33:16.412
All right.

33:29.758 --> 33:32.094
Your official title was?

33:35.306 --> 33:40.269
My name is Leonid Fedorovych Toptunov.

33:41.187 --> 33:46.442
I am the Senior Reactor Control
Chief Engineer

33:46.525 --> 33:48.527
at Chernobyl Nuclear Power Plant.

33:52.615 --> 33:54.533
Senior engineer?

33:56.869 --> 33:57.953
How old are you?

34:03.667 --> 34:05.044
I'm 25.

34:53.550 --> 34:55.552
Lyusya? Lyusya?

34:55.636 --> 34:57.888
Yes, I'm here, I'm here. I'm...

35:12.820 --> 35:14.238
Have you been here this whole time?

35:14.905 --> 35:16.365
No one said I should leave.

35:17.283 --> 35:18.325
I did.

35:18.993 --> 35:20.286
Thirty minutes, I said!

35:20.369 --> 35:23.330
Well, where have you been?
When he's in pain?

35:23.914 --> 35:25.457
When his sores stick to his gown?

35:25.541 --> 35:26.959
When he soils himself
five times a night?

35:27.042 --> 35:28.877
I've been looking after him.
Where have you been?

35:28.961 --> 35:30.671
I've been in the north and west wing,

35:30.754 --> 35:33.632
where there are dozens of patients
from Chernobyl exactly like him.

35:34.383 --> 35:35.968
- It isn't safe for you here.
- He's my husband.

35:36.051 --> 35:37.094
Not anymore.

35:37.177 --> 35:39.138
He's something else now.
Do you understand?

35:39.221 --> 35:40.514
He's dangerous to you.

35:41.807 --> 35:43.851
He's burned.

35:44.560 --> 35:45.894
Go home.

35:46.895 --> 35:47.938
Please.

35:51.483 --> 35:53.736
It won't take much longer. I, uh...

35:57.865 --> 35:59.491
I don't want him to die alone.

36:03.245 --> 36:04.913
Stay on the other side of the plastic,

36:07.041 --> 36:08.500
or I'll have you removed by security.

37:08.018 --> 37:09.645
- Lyusya?
- Yes, my love.

37:13.565 --> 37:14.650
Is it day?

37:16.110 --> 37:18.112
No, it's nighttime now.

37:22.241 --> 37:23.575
I think I had a dream,

37:24.159 --> 37:25.577
it's just gone.

37:27.788 --> 37:28.956
Vasya.

37:35.129 --> 37:36.839
We're going to have a baby.

38:13.876 --> 38:15.043
The fire's out.

38:17.754 --> 38:18.964
It's out, Valera.

38:20.674 --> 38:22.885
The miners are making
incredible progress.

38:24.386 --> 38:27.222
They say the whole job
will be finished in four weeks.

38:28.974 --> 38:29.975
Four weeks.

38:31.310 --> 38:32.394
Can you believe that?

38:39.151 --> 38:40.694
I know the job isn't over.

38:42.821 --> 38:44.364
But it's the beginning of the end.

38:50.454 --> 38:52.789
I'm sorry to bother you,
Deputy Minister,

38:55.417 --> 38:56.418
but it is the miners.

39:44.758 --> 39:45.801
What?

39:46.260 --> 39:48.554
You wouldn't give us fans,
it's too hot for clothes.

39:48.929 --> 39:51.348
So we're digging the old way.
This is the way our fathers mined.

39:54.017 --> 39:55.477
We're still wearing the fucking hats.

39:56.436 --> 39:57.521
What do you want?

40:00.649 --> 40:02.818
You're not as protected now.

40:03.569 --> 40:05.112
Are you telling me
it will make a difference?

40:11.159 --> 40:12.369
When this is over,

40:13.412 --> 40:14.621
will they be looked after?

40:18.917 --> 40:19.960
I don't know.

40:31.597 --> 40:32.598
You don't know.

40:52.200 --> 40:56.330
So the power level jumped
from 200 to 400 megawatts?

40:57.956 --> 40:58.999
Yes.

41:00.083 --> 41:01.209
Very fast.

41:03.003 --> 41:06.006
Why didn't you initiate
an emergency shutdown?

41:06.548 --> 41:08.842
Why didn't you press the AZ-5 button?

41:10.677 --> 41:11.678
We did.

41:12.929 --> 41:15.766
I reported the increase to Akimov,

41:15.849 --> 41:17.309
and he pressed the button.

41:18.977 --> 41:21.355
Leonid, that's... That's not possible.

41:23.607 --> 41:24.650
He did.

41:25.692 --> 41:26.943
I swear.

41:27.986 --> 41:29.404
I saw him do it.

41:33.325 --> 41:35.410
And that's when it exploded.

41:38.246 --> 41:39.247
What?

41:53.929 --> 41:54.930
Um...

41:56.264 --> 41:57.683
Which room is Akimov?

41:57.766 --> 41:58.767
Twenty-seven.

42:14.074 --> 42:17.452
I pressed it,
before the explosion.

42:17.953 --> 42:19.121
Before.

42:22.124 --> 42:23.417
But why?

42:24.668 --> 42:25.919
Why would that happen?

42:28.130 --> 42:31.007
I shut it down. I pressed AZ-5.

42:37.305 --> 42:38.724
Thank you, Comrade Akimov.

42:44.062 --> 42:45.564
I did everything right.

42:47.607 --> 42:49.025
I did everything right.

43:20.557 --> 43:21.600
Get out.

43:22.434 --> 43:23.727
Get out. Get out of here.

43:23.810 --> 43:26.146
Let me go! Let me go!

43:26.229 --> 43:28.523
Stop it! Stop it!

43:31.777 --> 43:34.404
You let her in that room?
Inside the plastic, touching him?

43:34.488 --> 43:35.864
Did you know she's pregnant?

43:35.947 --> 43:37.115
It's not true!

43:37.199 --> 43:38.408
What have you done?

43:38.492 --> 43:40.744
What kind of a place is this?
Where is her protection?

43:40.827 --> 43:42.954
Do you have any idea
what you're dealing with?

43:43.038 --> 43:44.831
- Of course, I do. Please, I do not...
- No.

43:45.707 --> 43:47.292
- People are going to hear about this.
- Wait.

43:47.709 --> 43:49.461
People are going to hear.
Do you understand?

43:49.544 --> 43:50.587
Everyone is going to hear.

43:51.421 --> 43:52.923
What is everyone gonna hear?

43:59.721 --> 44:01.723
I am with the official
Chernobyl Commission.

44:01.807 --> 44:04.017
I've been authorized
by Valery Legasov.

44:04.226 --> 44:05.227
You can check this.

44:05.310 --> 44:06.812
- My name is Ulana...
- We know who you are.

44:10.357 --> 44:11.942
What is everyone gonna hear?

44:33.338 --> 44:34.464
You have your notes?

44:35.215 --> 44:36.299
Yes.

44:39.261 --> 44:40.971
Khomyuk was arrested last night.

44:41.054 --> 44:43.306
What? Why?

44:43.390 --> 44:44.558
I don't know.

44:46.309 --> 44:47.394
Was it...

44:48.478 --> 44:49.479
Of course it was.

44:51.356 --> 44:52.440
I'm working on it.

44:53.066 --> 44:55.151
- Boris...
- I'm working on it.

44:56.570 --> 44:57.737
What more do you want from me?

44:58.738 --> 44:59.781
Fix your tie.

45:06.830 --> 45:07.873
They'll see you now.

45:18.508 --> 45:21.720
After thousands of sorties,
our brave helicopter crews

45:21.803 --> 45:24.014
successfully extinguished the fire.

45:24.097 --> 45:25.932
The miners are working
heroically to ensure

45:26.016 --> 45:28.476
that the fuel does not
reach the groundwater.

45:28.560 --> 45:32.272
And furthermore, there's no longer
a threat of additional explosion.

45:32.981 --> 45:36.776
The Soviet people have faced
the challenge and risen to the task,

45:37.152 --> 45:39.696
and they and everyone in this room
are to be commended.

45:44.993 --> 45:47.454
Lastly, Professor Legasov
and I have been vigilant

45:47.537 --> 45:49.873
to protect the security
interests of the State.

45:50.206 --> 45:52.626
And since the unfortunate
release of information

45:52.709 --> 45:54.461
directly following the accident,

45:54.544 --> 45:56.588
we believe that there
has been no further lapse.

45:57.130 --> 45:58.381
Comrade Charkov,

45:59.883 --> 46:03.178
we hope we have lived up to
the highest standards of the KGB.

46:03.595 --> 46:04.679
You have.

46:05.472 --> 46:06.514
Thank you.

46:07.891 --> 46:12.437
Professor Legasov will now speak
about the work that remains.

46:14.439 --> 46:15.565
Thank you.

46:19.861 --> 46:22.656
Deputy Chairman Shcherbina
has given you the good news,

46:22.739 --> 46:24.032
and it is good.

46:24.824 --> 46:26.952
The immediate danger is over.

46:27.535 --> 46:29.829
Now, I'm afraid,
a long war must begin.

46:32.040 --> 46:35.001
There is an enormous amount
of radioactive debris

46:35.085 --> 46:36.795
and contamination spread out
across a zone

46:36.878 --> 46:39.214
of approximately
2,600-square kilometers.

46:39.631 --> 46:43.635
This entire region must be
completely evacuated.

46:45.095 --> 46:48.306
We must go to every town,
every village to ensure this.

46:49.599 --> 46:54.562
And all animals still
surviving within the zone,

46:54.646 --> 46:57.399
whether domesticated or wild,

46:57.482 --> 47:01.903
must be presumed contaminated
and will have to be destroyed

47:01.987 --> 47:04.656
to prevent the spread
of radiation and disease.

47:06.032 --> 47:08.660
In the immediate area
surrounding Chernobyl,

47:08.743 --> 47:14.207
uh, every rock, every tree,
the very ground itself,

47:14.290 --> 47:17.919
has absorbed a dangerous
amount of radionuclides,

47:18.003 --> 47:21.381
which will be carried by the wind
and the rain if left exposed.

47:21.464 --> 47:23.633
So we will have to raze
entire forests.

47:23.717 --> 47:25.927
We will have to rip up
the top layer of earth

47:26.011 --> 47:27.387
and bury it under itself,

47:27.470 --> 47:30.473
approximately, 100 square kilometers.

47:32.767 --> 47:36.354
Um, and finally,
we will need to construct

47:36.438 --> 47:40.775
a containment structure
around the power plant itself,

47:40.859 --> 47:43.778
which will, of course,
still be extremely...

47:47.198 --> 47:48.950
There will be deaths.

47:52.620 --> 47:54.372
What amount of time,

47:54.456 --> 47:56.082
and how many men do you require?

47:56.332 --> 47:59.669
We expect this liquidation
effort to take three years

47:59.753 --> 48:02.338
and approximately 750,000 men,

48:02.422 --> 48:06.259
including a number of doctors
and structural engineers.

48:08.011 --> 48:09.304
How many deaths?

48:10.472 --> 48:11.723
Thousands.

48:12.515 --> 48:13.933
Perhaps tens of thousands.

48:22.317 --> 48:23.318
Begin at once.

48:29.699 --> 48:31.659
- Comrade Charkov.
- Valery!

48:33.787 --> 48:34.871
Yes, Professor?

48:36.122 --> 48:39.000
My associate was arrested last night.

48:39.542 --> 48:40.543
Oh?

48:41.419 --> 48:42.670
I mean no disrespect,

48:42.754 --> 48:44.714
but I was wondering
if you could tell me why.

48:44.798 --> 48:46.841
I assure you, I don't know
who you're talking about.

48:46.925 --> 48:48.843
She was arrested by the KGB.

48:50.011 --> 48:52.889
You are the first deputy
chairman of the KGB.

48:53.348 --> 48:54.349
I am.

48:54.724 --> 48:57.310
That's why I don't have to bother
with arresting people anymore.

48:57.393 --> 48:59.771
But you are bothering
with having us followed.

49:01.314 --> 49:04.025
I think the deputy chairman is busy.

49:04.109 --> 49:06.069
No, no. It's perfectly understandable.

49:06.402 --> 49:09.072
Comrade, I know you've heard
the stories about us.

49:10.156 --> 49:12.450
When I hear them, even I am shocked.

49:12.534 --> 49:14.494
But we are not what people say.

49:14.702 --> 49:16.788
Yes, people are following you.

49:17.455 --> 49:19.082
People are following those people.

49:19.999 --> 49:21.042
You see them?

49:23.586 --> 49:24.838
They follow me.

49:25.588 --> 49:29.008
The KGB is a circle of accountability.

49:29.342 --> 49:30.844
Nothing more.

49:31.010 --> 49:32.512
You know the work we're doing here.

49:34.639 --> 49:35.974
You really don't trust us?

49:36.057 --> 49:37.433
Of course, I do.

49:37.934 --> 49:39.811
But you know the old Russian proverb.

49:40.645 --> 49:42.105
"Trust but verify."

49:44.732 --> 49:48.278
And the Americans think that
Ronald Reagan thought that up.

49:48.361 --> 49:49.404
Can you imagine?

49:50.613 --> 49:52.240
It was very nice speaking with you.

49:53.533 --> 49:54.742
I need her.

49:57.453 --> 49:59.914
So you will be accountable for her?

50:04.544 --> 50:05.628
Then it's done.

50:07.130 --> 50:09.048
- Her name is...
- I know who she is.

50:10.133 --> 50:11.467
Good day, Professor.

50:21.769 --> 50:24.814
Well, that went surprisingly well.

50:25.648 --> 50:27.317
You came off like a naive idiot.

50:29.027 --> 50:31.279
And naive idiots are not a threat.

50:47.295 --> 50:49.255
I'll come back when
the paperwork's complete.

50:57.639 --> 50:58.765
Are you all right?

50:58.848 --> 51:00.058
They didn't hurt me.

51:02.310 --> 51:04.729
They let a pregnant woman
into a room with a...

51:04.896 --> 51:06.856
It doesn't matter.

51:08.149 --> 51:09.901
They were stupid. I was stupid.

51:12.237 --> 51:13.571
Dyatlov won't talk to me.

51:15.365 --> 51:17.700
Akimov, yes, Toptunov, yes, but...

51:19.911 --> 51:21.079
Valery,

51:21.663 --> 51:22.789
Akimov...

51:24.207 --> 51:25.500
His face was gone.

51:28.878 --> 51:30.088
You want to stop?

51:32.382 --> 51:34.133
Is that a choice I even have?

51:42.976 --> 51:46.145
Do you think the fuel will actually
melt through the concrete pad?

51:46.229 --> 51:49.440
I don't know. A 40% chance, maybe.

51:52.652 --> 51:54.529
I said 50.

51:55.530 --> 51:57.657
Either way, the numbers
mean the same thing.

51:57.740 --> 51:58.825
"Maybe."

52:02.120 --> 52:04.622
Maybe the core will melt
through to the groundwater.

52:05.581 --> 52:07.834
Maybe the miners who I've told
to dig under the reactor

52:07.917 --> 52:09.585
will save millions of lives.

52:11.546 --> 52:13.172
Maybe I'm killing them for nothing.

52:17.427 --> 52:19.095
I don't want to do this anymore.

52:21.055 --> 52:22.223
I want to stop.

52:24.267 --> 52:25.351
But I can't.

52:27.186 --> 52:29.647
I don't think you have
a choice any more than I do.

52:31.649 --> 52:34.444
I think, despite the stupidity,

52:35.069 --> 52:36.904
the lies, even this,

52:37.864 --> 52:39.157
you are compelled.

52:40.158 --> 52:42.535
The problem has been assigned,
and you will stop at nothing

52:42.618 --> 52:43.911
until you find an answer.

52:43.995 --> 52:46.622
Because that is who you are.

52:48.875 --> 52:50.168
A lunatic, then.

52:52.754 --> 52:53.755
A scientist.

53:16.027 --> 53:18.279
Did you know that they were
running a safety test?

53:20.156 --> 53:21.157
Yeah.

53:21.240 --> 53:22.367
There's something else.

53:24.243 --> 53:27.413
Akimov says
they shut the reactor down,

53:27.497 --> 53:29.415
and Toptunov confirms it.

53:30.083 --> 53:31.250
They pressed AZ-5.

53:31.542 --> 53:33.252
Apparently not soon enough.

53:33.753 --> 53:34.837
No.

53:35.463 --> 53:39.258
They say Akimov pressed AZ-5,

53:40.134 --> 53:42.095
and then the reactor exploded.

53:44.430 --> 53:47.183
If it had been just one of them,
I would have put it under

53:47.266 --> 53:50.144
faulty memory or delusion even,

53:50.228 --> 53:52.939
but they both agreed.
They were adamant.

53:57.568 --> 53:58.653
Comrade?

54:01.697 --> 54:02.782
Do you think it's possible?

54:02.865 --> 54:04.450
I think it makes no sense. I...

54:05.201 --> 54:08.413
I think it's what I would say if
I was trying to cover my own mistakes.

54:09.038 --> 54:10.039
But?

54:11.290 --> 54:12.458
I believe them.

54:15.294 --> 54:16.712
Then you should pursue it.

54:17.338 --> 54:19.966
We have to pursue every possibility,

54:20.842 --> 54:22.677
no matter how unlikely,

54:23.511 --> 54:25.847
no matter what or who's to blame.

54:28.141 --> 54:31.394
I'll go back to the hospital
and re-interview Akimov and Toptunov.

54:34.897 --> 54:35.982
If they're still awake.

54:37.775 --> 54:38.818
They're not.

54:41.154 --> 54:42.155
Khomyuk.
